WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.320
Turkmenistan - A central Asian nation near the&nbsp;
Caspian sea - known for its rivaling nomadic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:13.440
tribes, make it a commonplace for rising conflict&nbsp;
more often than not. But in Western Turkmenistan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.880
a small group of eight&nbsp;
rather peculiar tribes exist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.880
While at first glance, they may seem&nbsp;
to be just another group of nomads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.480
posing no threat to anyone aside from the other&nbsp;
opposing tribes in the immediate area, they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:32.880
anything but ordinary. Shrouded in mystery, it&nbsp;
is of SCP Foundation belief that they may be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.800
a significant threat due to the many questions&nbsp;
still unanswered regarding their origins.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.080
The most dire question of all isn’t&nbsp;
where they came from - but when.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:51.120
SCP-3838 - Nomads of the 4th-Dimensional&nbsp;
Steppe is a collection of eight nomadic tribes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.480
occupying a small area of ten kilometers.&nbsp;
They all seem to be of similar origin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:01.680
but they are very different in behavior and in&nbsp;
the way that they interact with outsiders. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:07.920
multiple tribes can share the same space, they&nbsp;
don’t all exist in the space at the same time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.800
Periodically, the current tribe will perform&nbsp;
a ritual. With two flames near the entrance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:18.800
they will enter a yurt - and vanish. They&nbsp;
will soon be replaced by another tribe.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.280
This new tribe will appear, seemingly&nbsp;
having traveled from another time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.600
though the Foundation is unable to&nbsp;
determine how exactly this ritual works.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:33.040
All the tribes typically survive off the goats&nbsp;
and sheep in the area, and live in huts. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:39.200
religions and traditions vary. Each group has its&nbsp;
own Khan and speaks the same dialect of Turkmen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.360
but interaction with the groups has&nbsp;
led to some bizarre revelations.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.960
For one thing, their dialect was last&nbsp;
commonly spoken in the fifteenth century.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:54.320
Some of these groups are humble traders. Others&nbsp;
are hostile and warlike. And the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:59.680
rarely knows which they’ll be dealing with next.&nbsp;
While these groups all occupy the same place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.800
but not the same time, they have&nbsp;
developed unique ways around this issue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:09.280
The tribes seem to treat time the&nbsp;
same way other groups treat location,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:13.760
forming treaties that allow them to&nbsp;
benefit when they switch into the space.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.000
But while some choose peace, others choose war.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.840
Observations made by the Foundation have&nbsp;
proven that when a new tribe appears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.800
violence and attacks from them are not only&nbsp;
common, but have been growing significantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:33.200
more volatile over time. Unlike many SCPs, the&nbsp;
Nomads of the 4th Dimensional Steppe are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:39.600
new. They have been occupying this land since at&nbsp;
least 1696, when they were first sighted. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.600
initial sightings were not made by the&nbsp;
Foundation - which at that time, didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.200
exist in its current form. It was after a massive&nbsp;
battle approximately three millennia earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:55.280
that The Devan-e-Jaaduyih, or Office of Magic,&nbsp;
picked up reports of disappearing tents.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.760
Over the years, they have slowly but consistently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:03.760
amassed more and more knowledge of the&nbsp;
eight tribes now designated as SCP-3838.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.040
Each tribe exists in the same geographic space,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.520
but they come from a different era of history&nbsp;
- and bring with them different culture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:17.360
traditions, technology, and weaponry. The space&nbsp;
itself changed drastically, from its earliest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:23.760
days as a holy site in the 15th century BCE,&nbsp;
to a bustling marketplace in the 1800s. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.800
marketplace is of particular interest to the&nbsp;
Foundation, as it is said to possess strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.720
and magical items like guns that shoot bolts of&nbsp;
light and arrows that follow their targets. Both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:40.400
the 15th century holy site and the marketplace&nbsp;
are unique locations in time - they are the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:46.000
only two places that manifest where the tribes&nbsp;
interact and hold councils and negotiations. 
 &nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.960
Each of these tribes bring unique challenges&nbsp;
and opportunities for the Foundation.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:58.160
SCP-3838-1 is one of the smallest tribes, a humble&nbsp;
group of vendors. They only appear in the communal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:03.840
marketplace in the 18th century, but are believed&nbsp;
to be from the second and third century CE,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.880
and they are known as excellent potters. If&nbsp;
you see them, the odds are they’re trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.920
sell you some nice earthenware pots. But while&nbsp;
they’re not relevant to the larger conflict,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:20.080
they are a unique group for one reason - they&nbsp;
follow the Manichean religion instead of Islam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:24.720
and are strong believers in the religion’s&nbsp;
dualist battle between good and evil - the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:30.720
latter being associated with the color red.
The second tribe has something unique.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:38.160
SCP-3838-2 originates from closer to our&nbsp;
time, between the 12th and 18th century CE,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:44.160
and they are the only tribe led entirely by women.&nbsp;
This matriarchal society participates in all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:49.840
standard tribal activities, including combat&nbsp;
and herding, and their lore speaks of a female&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:55.200
warrior who led in the initial great battle&nbsp;
thousands of years ago. Their territory is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.480
among the largest of the tribes, but little is&nbsp;
known about them beyond that. They practice a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:06.720
mix of traditional shamanism and Islam, and are&nbsp;
known for a ritual hunt with roots in Mongolia.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.680
These women warriors are fierce, but&nbsp;
not at the center of the conflict.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.720
But the tribes that grow closer to the&nbsp;
present day hold much more territory.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:26.240
SCP-3838-3 is the current tribe, occupying the&nbsp;
land from between 1870 and 2054 CE - into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:31.440
future. It’s a simple tribe that seems to have&nbsp;
moved closer to a modern system of government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:36.640
Its Khan leads alongside a collection of lesser&nbsp;
governors advising him. The tribe is known for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:41.520
their carpet-weaving skills, with their stunning&nbsp;
wares being a popular item for bartering in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:47.840
marketplace. But this group previously held much&nbsp;
more territory. Their position as a dominant force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:53.680
is being threatened by a powerful force.
And that force is getting closer.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:06:01.840
SCP-3838-4 is believed to occupy the land from&nbsp;
between 2054 and 3000 - the longest-lasting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:07.520
tribe - and they didn’t get there by negotiations&nbsp;
and bartering. This tribe is feared by all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:14.240
other tribes, the only one not welcome in the&nbsp;
communal spaces, and it’s not hard to see why.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:20.160
They’re hostile and warlike, attacking both other&nbsp;
tribes and Foundation members. If you look closely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:26.160
at them - and are able to survive - you might&nbsp;
see that they’re dressed in human skins. Those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:31.440
captured by them who survive are likely to wind&nbsp;
up as their slaves, which makes their army large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:37.200
and virtually unconquerable. Their traditions&nbsp;
are mostly unknown, but they seem focused on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:43.760
a funeral urn they protect at all costs - which&nbsp;
they claim contains the body of a fallen enemy.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:49.520
But no empire lasts forever, and&nbsp;
something new will eventually rise.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:56.880
SCP-3838-5 took over the space from 3000 to&nbsp;
3020, after the fall of their predecessors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.680
and they couldn’t be more different. This small,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:04.080
peaceful tribe has few members left&nbsp;
and is mostly seen at the marketplace.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.800
They’re known for being excellent cooks and&nbsp;
have good relations with most other tribes. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:13.920
Foundation is more likely to encounter them in the&nbsp;
Marketplace than in their own territory - which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:18.960
is rapidly shrinking and barely has enough&nbsp;
room to farm or to build new settlements.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.640
But the tribes were about to take a quantum leap.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:27.760
The source of the strange and powerful weapons&nbsp;
at the Marketplace was a mystery - until the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:34.960
Foundation met SCP-3838-6. This&nbsp;
tribe ruled from 3020 to 3450,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:40.160
and were closely aligned with their predecessors.&nbsp;
A traditional Shi’ite muslim group unconcerned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:45.600
with the mysticism of the other tribes,&nbsp;
their technology is powerful and advanced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:51.120
and they work with a secretive group called the&nbsp;
Empire for the Reclaimation of Islamic Artifacts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:55.840
Due to their advanced culture and intellectual&nbsp;
nature, they’re the most common point group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:00.000
for interaction with the Foundation&nbsp;
- They are friendly and cooperative,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.800
and the Foundation is careful to keep it that&nbsp;
way rather than meet them on the battlefield.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:08.240
The next tribe is a mystery.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:14.720
Originally, SCP-3838-7&nbsp;
existed from 3500 to 4100 CE.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:20.080
They were a powerful and long-lasting&nbsp;
empire - but every empire ends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:25.120
and this one came to a crashing halt in a&nbsp;
conquest that eliminated all their territory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:30.880
and left them as simple nomads, lost in time&nbsp;
and mostly existing within the marketplace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:39.200
and as refugees within the other tribes. Or, when&nbsp;
it comes to the warlike SCP-3838-4, as captives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:46.480
The majority can be found within the small group&nbsp;
of SCP-3838-5. But the question remains - what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:53.440
brought this tribe to an end? Most stories of this&nbsp;
period attribute the destruction to SCP-3838-4.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:57.040
But recent events may tell a different story.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:05.120
SCP-3838-8 is the most mysterious tribe of all&nbsp;
- and for good reason - we do not know when they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:11.600
begin or end. They come from the far future, and&nbsp;
none of the other tribes communicate with them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:18.320
In fact, no members of SCP-3838-8 have ever been&nbsp;
encountered - however all of the other tribes know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:23.840
of them, and many refer to them as the enemy at&nbsp;
the great battle. But no tribe hates them more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:31.760
than the warriors of SCP-3838-4, who know them as&nbsp;
the enemy above all enemies. And unfortunately due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:39.280
to SCP-3838-4’s warlike nature, the Foundation has&nbsp;
learned very little about this mysterious rival.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.680
That is, until 2011.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:48.400
Contact with SCP-3838-4 is rare, especially&nbsp;
non-hostile contact. Which is why it was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:53.520
surprise when a member of the tribe approached&nbsp;
the nearby research base with no army and no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:59.040
weapons. He claimed to be an envoy - a rarity&nbsp;
for a tribe with little use for diplomats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:04.400
But he wanted to speak with the site director, and&nbsp;
thus, he was granted an interview with Dr. Rizvi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:09.440
The tribesman was uncommunicative and reserved&nbsp;
at first. It seemed as though he was having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:14.400
trouble trusting Dr. Rizvi, but after a bit&nbsp;
of prodding by the doctor, the envoy warmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.960
up to him and began to speak.
What he shared was shocking.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:25.440
There was a long history of mistrust between&nbsp;
the Foundation and SCP-3838-4, with many deaths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:30.720
on both sides. But the Envoy was now insisting&nbsp;
that there had been a purpose for their raids.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:34.320
He even seemed to regret the killings&nbsp;
of other tribes and referred to them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:40.000
as “Brother.”. But he was there for a purpose.&nbsp;
He wanted to talk about the great battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:46.960
and he referred to the aftermath, this strange&nbsp;
place out of time, not as a tribe or as territory.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:48.240
But as a prison.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:53.600
He claimed that they were imprisoning something&nbsp;
in a pocket of time - and something else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:59.200
another part of the whole, in another&nbsp;
reality. And they were the only ones who knew.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:02.720
They guarded it ruthlessly,&nbsp;
and they guarded it alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:09.520
Their only partner in this lonely battle was&nbsp;
SCP-3838-7, and their tribe was gone now. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:14.880
burden was such that the other tribes would see&nbsp;
them as bloodthirsty monsters - but they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:20.240
anything but. They were the ones keeping&nbsp;
the actual bloodthirsty monsters at bay.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.800
At least that was the story he gave,&nbsp;
while wearing the skins of his enemies.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:28.720
It was impossible to make a firm deal&nbsp;
because of the lack of information,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:33.440
but the Envoy was desperate. He claimed he&nbsp;
was bound by a higher power to not tell the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:37.760
full story, but he asked the Foundation&nbsp;
to serve as an intermediary to help them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:44.320
unite the tribes. His desperation was clear - Dr.&nbsp;
Rizvi was still skeptical, but he agreed to meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:49.600
with the other tribes. In the end, the tribes&nbsp;
were able to receive agreed upon concessions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:55.520
and in return, SCP-3838-4 stopped&nbsp;
its campaign of warlike expansion.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:12:00.080
All seemed to be well - until&nbsp;
a new document was discovered.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:05.280
Foundation operative John Callaghan was involved&nbsp;
in the Marketplace period during the 19th century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:08.960
and he wrote down a translation&nbsp;
of a song he heard repeatedly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:15.440
While it was known by many tribes, legend had&nbsp;
it that it originated with SCP-3838-8 - one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:20.560
the only known pieces of culture from the&nbsp;
mysterious tribe. It spoke of a mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:26.160
being named the Crimson Khan who one day&nbsp;
would return when seven seals were opened.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.880
They forget the hallowed&nbsp;
words upon the death of time.&nbsp;

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:36.160
May they share the fate of those&nbsp;
who deny to me what's mine,&nbsp;

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:40.320
They forget the howling&nbsp;
chains that bind me safe away,&nbsp;

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:44.880
One of many old chanyus forgotten in this way.&nbsp;

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:50.480
They forget the steel swords&nbsp;
they used to cast me down,&nbsp;

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:55.600
They shall not forget again&nbsp;
before my flaming crown.&nbsp;

00:12:55.600 --> 00:13:00.160
They forget the seven brides&nbsp;
that wait for my return,&nbsp;

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:04.720
Such loveliness is lost upon&nbsp;
the children of the urns.&nbsp;

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:09.280
They forget the seals that&nbsp;
are used to keep me still,&nbsp;

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:14.320
Only one remembers and is not bent to my will.&nbsp;

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:22.560
Seven seals, seven tribes, six&nbsp;
reclaimed, one shall be mine,&nbsp;

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:28.880
And ere the end of all your days&nbsp;
the Crimson Khan shall ride.

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:35.360
But who is the Crimson Khan? Researchers note a&nbsp;
lot of similarities between this unknown entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:41.040
and the Scarlet King, one of the SCP-001&nbsp;
proposals. Could they be one and the same?

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:45.120
The Foundation is keeping a close eye on&nbsp;
the situation, with a perimeter established&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:49.120
one kilometer away from the tribes’&nbsp;
territory. One entrance is available&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:53.920
for contact between the Foundation and the&nbsp;
tribes, but the perimeter is heavily armed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.920 --> 00:14:00.880
in case SCP-3838-4 gets aggressive again&nbsp;
- or in case any other threat emerges.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:07.280
The focus is on diplomatic relations with&nbsp;
the current occupying tribe of SCP-3883-3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:11.520
but there are continued efforts at engaging&nbsp;
the tribe that will be their successor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:16.320
The Foundation has a hands-off policy with&nbsp;
regards to conflicts between the tribes.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:18.800
With one exception.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:24.160
The Foundation is keeping a close eye&nbsp;
out for any members of SCP-3838-8,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:29.360
with orders to detain and interrogate them&nbsp;
on sight. But none have ever been seen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:35.600
and in fact, the Foundation doesn’t even know what&nbsp;
to look for. If they’re as powerful as believed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:42.080
given their feared reputation, they may already&nbsp;
be here, infiltrating the other tribes. But the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:46.880
Foundation is determined to learn more about&nbsp;
them, and whatever they’re bringing with them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:53.200
They just hope to do it before the Crimson Khan&nbsp;
- whoever he may be - makes his presence known.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:59.200
For more on another mysterious and dangerous&nbsp;
group, check out “SCP-1861 - The Crew of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:07.760
HMS Wintersheimer”, or watch “SCP-4007 - Unit&nbsp;
731” for another unusual group of warriors.

